0347: SapphireGpu: DDR voted with the GPU level, as kgsl votes its bus path (kern.sweet_gpu_ddr, default 0)

No vote unless kern.sweet_gpu_ddr=1 (boot-arg gpu_ddr=1). Needs 0343 and 0345.

kgsl votes the path GPU -> DDR at every level change (ib from qcom,bus-table-ddr of the level, ab 25 % of
ib); the interconnect driver turns it into a BIMC rate for the RPM: max(ab sum, ib) / 8 bytes, in kHz. So
the vote is ib / 8: 534180 kHz at 320 MHz, 750000 at 465, 993164 at 600, 1518555 at 785, 1761719 at 1025,
2042969 at 1114.8 and 1260 (820 and 980 take 1025's, 1100 takes 1114.8's). This driver sends that rate
itself (RPM "clk2" 0, key "KHz", active set), never under kern.sweet_gpu_ddr_floor (kHz, 0), from
opp_votes(): going up after the rails and before the clock, going down after the clock. A refused vote is
counted and leaves the old one.

kern.sweet_gpu_ddr: 1 votes for the current rate at once and at every change; 0 votes INT_MAX, what the stock
clock driver leaves on the BIMC at probe. Each sysctl write measures the DDR (0343) before and 20 ms after.
kern.sweet_gpu_ddr_stats (read only): mode, floor, the vote in place and its GPU rate, votes, refusals, the
last answer, the DDR before/after and now.

While the RPM's clock scaling is off (nothing in this kernel turns it on; 0361 does) a vote is expected to
change nothing. Measured (n=1 per rate): votes of 1761719 kHz (GPU at 820 MHz) and 2042969 kHz (1260 MHz)
answered 0 by the RPM, DDR at 1555210 kHz before and 20 ms after in both.
Checked on the host with 0345's model plus a clk2 resource: vote per level, kgsl's order around the PLL,
floor, refused vote, INT_MAX when switched off.

